text:
sam: Hey team — hitting intermittent 401s from the Edge TS SDK when deployed to Cloudflare Pages Functions. Works fine locally (dev server) but in prod ~10-20% of requests to the Redwood API get a 401. Quick repro and logs below.

sam: Middleware we run on every request (simplified):
```js
export async function onRequest(context) {
  const { env, request } = context;
  const resp = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'authorization': `Bearer ${env.REDWOOD_KEY}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'hi' }),
    credentials: 'include'
  });
  return resp;
}
```

sam: Prod log snippet: `fetch https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -> 401`
sam: Response headers (sometimes):
```
access-control-allow-origin: *
access-control-expose-headers: x-request-id
content-type: application/json
```
sam: Notice `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` is missing (we do need credentials on some flows).

ingrid: Thanks — can you paste the SDK version + your bundler/build config? Also are you deploying as Cloudflare Pages Functions or Pages with a background worker?

sam: Using `@redwood/inference-js@0.8.3`. Build: webpack 5 with `esbuild-loader` (default CF Pages build). target currently not set (defaults to `web`).

alex: Hm — common pattern: bundlers accidentally polyfill node `fetch` or inject `node-fetch` shims which break the runtime's native credentials handling in webworker/edge environments. Also some older SDK builds emitted code that depended on a Node-style Request normalization — we fixed a header serialization bug in later SDKs for edge builds.

maria: Confirming: we shipped an edge-specific fix in 0.8.4 that addressed intermittent header dropping when bundled with certain tools. If upgrading is possible try `npm i @redwood/inference-js@^0.8.4`.

alex: Meanwhile you can also force the bundler to keep the native `fetch` by changing the webpack target to `webworker` (Cloudflare) or `web` for Vercel Edge. Example webpack snippet:
```js
// webpack.config.js
module.exports = {
  target: 'webworker', // ensures no node-fetch polyfills for Pages Functions
  resolve: {
    fallback: {
      stream: false,
      buffer: false,
      'node-fetch': false
    }
  },
};
```

alex: If you can't change target, check the final bundle for `require('node-fetch')` or small `fetch` shims.

sam: Tried upgrading to 0.8.4 locally — tests pass. Deployed with webpack `target: 'webworker'` as suggested and initial smoke looks good. Will monitor for the intermittent 401s.

sam: Quick manual repro I ran (before the fix):
```
curl -i -X OPTIONS https://<pages-url>/.netlify/functions/app -H 'Origin: https://example.com' -H 'Access-Control-Request-Method: POST'
```
The preflight reply used to omit `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` and had weird header ordering in some responses.

maria: That's helpful — can you open a support ticket if you see it again and include a capture of the bundle (search for `node-fetch` or `__fetch__` strings) + the exact webpack config? We can push a canary edge build to validate.

support-bot: Created ticket RDW-8721 for `sam` with label `edge-401-intermittent` — please add recordings and bundle if you can.

sam: Will attach bundle + `webpack.config.js` there if it flares up again. Thanks all, switching the target fixed the immediate repro. :thumbsup:
